<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SEA HARVEST BOOSTS HEADLINE EPS BY 21 PCT.</title>
<headline>SEA HARVEST BOOSTS HEADLINE EPS BY 21 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31,</p>
<p>1997</p>
<p>			 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)	    26.4    vs	   21.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			  10.0    vs	    9.0</p>
<p>    Attrib			    27.902   vs	  23.683</p>
<p>    Operating profit		41.756   vs	  31.258</p>
<p>    Profit before tax	     49.819   vs	  41.618</p>
<p>    Tax				 19.559   vs	  16.231</p>
<p>    Profit after tax		30.260   vs	  25.367</p>
<p>    Loss by associate	    (2.519)   vs	 (1.704)</p>
<p>    Turnover			 238.202   vs	 184.999</p>
<p>Div payable July 1</p>
<p>on register May 30</p>
<p>Full name: Sea Harvest Corporation Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had suffered an increase in</p>
<p>losses from its Namibian associate from 1.7 million rand to 2.5</p>
<p>million rand due to a reduction in the total allowable catch and</p>
<p>poor fishing conditions in Namibian waters.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
